 LAP would typically be expected", "Myelodysplastic syndrome with cytopenias and elevated LAP: less likely given age and lack of marrow fibrosis signs", "Hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis: requires more specific fever/cytopenia correlation and organomegaly, which are not present"], "alarm_features": ["Unexplained weight loss", "Elevated WBC with thrombocytopenia and anemia (pancytopenia with leukocytosis)", "Elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal differential in leukocytosis argues against acute processes like AML/blast crisis, favoring chronic MPNs."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4409767587381611, "posterior": 0.5575626578265024, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP is a key feature of CML, strengthening B2's plausibility while ruling out infection/reactive causes."], "evidence_against": ["Thrombocytopenia is atypical for CML in chronic/accelerated phase, reducing B2's likelihood but not ruling out blast crisis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "time_course", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and normal lymphocyte count we