onsistent with B2.3, though this evidence is weaker than t…"]}}, "frontier": ["B2.1", "B2.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated LAP and normal lymphocyte count in the differential disfavor lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders (B3) as the diagnosis?", "summary": "Elevated LAP and normal lymphocyte count make lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders (B3) unlikely, as they typically present with lymphocytosis and normal LAP."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated LAP and subacute symptom onset (fatigue over weeks) strongly support CML (B2.1) over other MPNs (B2.3)?", "summary": "Elevated LAP is a characteristic feature of CML in chronic/accelerated phase, providing moderate support for B2.1 and strong exclusion of B2.3."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the anemia and thrombocytopenia with absence of erythrocytosis support primary myelofibrosis (B2.2) over other MPNs (B2.3)?", "summary": "Anemia and thrombocytopenia without erythrocytosis slightly favor myelofibrosis (B2.2) but remain inconsistent with B2.3, though this evidence is weaker than the LAP finding."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly in the physical exam argue against CML in chronic/accelerated phase (B2.1)?", "summary": "Lack of splenomegaly weakly reduces the likelihood of CML in chronic/accelerated phase (B2.1), which commonly presents with splenomegaly."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of marrow fibrosis signs (splenomegaly, extramedullary hematopoiesis) in the physical exam disfavor primary myelofibrosis (B2.2)?", "summary": "Absence of marrow fibrosis signs weakly disfavors primary myelofibrosis (B2.2), which typically presents with splenomegaly."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated LAP and normal lymphocyte count in the differential disfa